1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
[bird screeches]

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
This is it, Gon. My brother sent the URL.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,000
That’s awesome! Let’s get started!

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Yeah!

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
[theme song playing]

6
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
GATHERING x OF x HEROES

7
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
[narrator] As Kurapika
sets out on the path

8
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,000
to face the Phantom Troupe
and avenge the Kurta,

9
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Gon and Killua are also busy

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,000
making their own preparations
for the auction in Yorknew City.

11
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:57,000
INTERNET CAFÉ

12
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[Gon] Is this the Hunter website?

13
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Yeah. I’ve heard that Hunters worldwide
post lots of information here.

14
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Worldwide? Really?

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,000
That’s pretty amazing.

16
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,000
[computer]
Please swipe your Hunter’s License

17
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:22,000
and enter your license code.

18
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,000
[beeps]

19
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:28,000
[Gon typing]

20
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
[door creaking]

21
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[Killua]
Put the cursor on the bartender.

22
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
[bartender]
What kind of information do you want?

23
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Wow! That’s a lot of info!

24
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Click "game category."

25
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
There it is. Greed Island.

26
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Price is 20 million Jenny.

27
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
Twenty million?

28
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:59,000
I guess they won’t give out information
for free.

29
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,000
All right. I guess we gotta.

30
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Okay then, I’m depositing 20 million.

31
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
I can feel aura coming from the monitor!

32
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Then to enter the site...

33
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:18,000
it looks like you actually
have to be a Nen user.

34
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Okay. Now listen very carefully.

35
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Y’see, Greed Island

36
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
is a game created by Nen users.

37
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
It appears that there are
multiple creators

38
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
whose motives are unclear.

39
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:37,000
They infused Nen into
all hundred copies of the game.

40
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Nen activates on startup,

41
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
pulling the player inside the game itself.

42
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Wait. Inside the game?

43
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
[bartender]
Only Nen users can actually play it.

44
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:51,000
As long as the player stays alive
within the game,

45
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
the console will continue to run,
even if the game is unplugged.

46
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
It will stop if the player dies.

47
00:03:58,000 --> 00:03:59,000
There was one owner...

48
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:03,000
who hired fifty Hunters to give it a shot.

49
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
And of the 50...

50
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
not a single one ever came back.

51
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
I heard you can return
if you can find a save point.

52
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:15,000
Is that true?

53
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,000
It’s from the Hunter website.

54
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:18,000
It’s gotta be accurate.

55
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:21,000
At the Yorknew City auction,

56
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
there are going to be
seven units of Greed Island

57
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
and every one of them
will be available for purchase.

58
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:32,000
Of course, the lowest starting bid
is 8.9 billion Jenny.

59
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
8.9 billion?

60
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
The price has skyrocketed!

61
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
That’s three billion more
than we’d pay for retail!

62
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
Getting one’s ranked level G.

63
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,000
[both] Huh?

64
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
The game is considered a legend,

65
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:47,000
but there are still
plenty of units around.

66
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,000
If you have enough money,

67
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
it should be relatively easy
to procure one.

68
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Hmm... A G-rank, huh?

69
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
That’s lower than I thought.

70
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,000
You’re telling me, if I can’t even
get my hands on a simple game,

71
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:02,000
I’ll never be able to find you.

72
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,000
Right, Ging?

73
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:12,000
[Killua] Still, the money’s a big problem.

74
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Hey. This auction…

75
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Do you think
that we can participate in it?

76
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
At 8.9 billion?

77
00:05:19,000 --> 00:05:21,000
C’mon, that’s way out of our league!

78
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Uh-huh. Not to go buy stuff, but to sell.

79
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Selling, huh? That’s it!

80
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
We can go look for treasure

81
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
and then auction off
whatever we manage to find.

82
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Yes!

83
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:35,000
We can start with the 800 million
that we earned fighting at Heavens Arena

84
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,000
and go from there.

85
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Hmm.

86
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:39,000
First off,

87
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:42,000
we’ll try the online flea markets
and auction websites.

88
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,000
Now, let’s see what we can dig up.

89
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:51,000
We’ll increase our funds
and then, get a copy of Greed Island!

90
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Yeah!

91
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
-Yeah!
-All right!

92
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,000
[both laughing]

93
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,000
How much... is left?

94
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:27,000
Between the two of us,
we’re at 10.84 million.

95
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,000
[both sigh]

96
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
What the hell?

97
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
When we first started,
we were making a decent amount.

98
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
I knew this would happen.

99
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
That’s why I told you
we should stick to the reputable sites.

100
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
I couldn’t help myself!

101
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
The risky sites are the only real way
to make a profit!

102
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:46,000
[both sigh]

103
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
This isn’t working out so good.

104
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[man] Now, then…

105
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
show me what you’ve brought.

106
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Hair from the famous actress, Sara.

107
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
DNA authenticated.

108
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:03,000
Taken from an Egypersian pyramid.

109
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
It’s a mummy’s right arm.

110
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
The Scaly skin of a Dracoderma patient.

111
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
The skull of a unicorn tribesman.

112
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Okay, then.

113
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Congratulations,
all four of you are hired.

114
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:20,000
My name is Dalzollene,
the head bodyguard.

115
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,000
You start now.

116
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,000
I look forward
to working with each of you.

117
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Your mission

118
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:30,000
is to safely escort the boss
to a Yorknew City hotel room.

119
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
A private airship
will take you all to Lingon,

120
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:36,000
an airport outside of Yorknew.

121
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
From the airport, it’s ninety minutes

122
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
to get to the hotel.

123
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
A car will be waiting.

124
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:46,000
The four of you will be assigned
to provide the outer ring of security.

125
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,000
Any questions?

126
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Do you know
who might be targeting the boss?

127
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:54,000
That question’s not deserving
of an answer.

128
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
[Kurapika] What do you mean?

129
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
The boss is a VIP in the underworld.

130
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:01,000
There are plenty who hold a grudge.

131
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Since you didn’t understand,
I’ll rephrase.

132
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
Grudges aside,

133
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:09,000
can you think of anyone
who might actually commit to an attack?

134
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Anyone at all?

135
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
If we can identify the candidates,
their styles and motives,

136
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
we can prepare…

137
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
helping us to ensure
the boss’s protection.

138
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[Dalzollene] Kurapika, is it?

139
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
You are the one who doesn’t understand.

140
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,000
Our job is to protect the boss,

141
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:32,000
no matter who, when,
where or how they attack.

142
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,000
That's all you need to know! Got it?

143
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
So, don’t bother
building a mental profile.

144
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Everyone who approaches is an enemy.

145
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:48,000
It’s time to meet the boss.

146
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Come on.

147
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:03,000
[Baise] Excuse me. What’s that?

148
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
[Basho] It’s a little too realistic.

149
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
-That is an actual human being.
-[all gasp]

150
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
He used to be a fellow bodyguard.

151
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:19,000
But he ignored my advice
and was fooled by false information,

152
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:23,000
putting the other bodyguards
and the boss at risk.

153
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
And so, he was punished accordingly.

154
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,000
You were all brought in
to be his replacements.

155
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Let's go.

156
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Boss. I’ve brought the new bodyguards.

157
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Come in.

158
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[Dalzollene] The boss, Miss Neon.

159
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
[all four gasp]

160
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:05,000
[giggles] New hires!
It’s a pleasure to meet you!

161
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
[Basho] Well, anyway,

162
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
I was pretty surprised
when we met the boss.

163
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
[Baise] No kidding.

164
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
They called her an important figure
in the underworld,

165
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
so I thought it’d be someone intimidating,

166
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
but she turned out to be
a cute little girl.

167
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,000
[footsteps approaching]

168
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,000
[both] Huh?

169
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Pakunoda! Hey, how’ve you been?

170
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
[Pakunoda] Long time no see, Shalnark.

171
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:05,000
You too, Phinks.

172
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
[snorts]
You sure took your time getting here.

173
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:11,000
Oh? Right on time by my watch.

174
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:14,000
You were supposed to arrive here
ten minutes early.

175
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,000
Same for you guys.

176
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
[Shalnark] Bonolenov! Kortopi!

177
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
So, you’re going with us, too?

178
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,000
[man] Hey!

179
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Haven’t seen you in quite a while.

180
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
I’m reporting for duty, boss.

181
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:33,000
What’s our target this time?

182
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
I’m itchin’ for our new orders!

183
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:37,000
[Shalnark chuckles] Easy now, Uvo.

184
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Feitan’s group won’t be arriving
until evening.

185
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:42,000
We’ll wait until everyone’s here.

186
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[Pakunoda] Impatient as usual.

187
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Damn. That’s an entire
half day of waiting.

188
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Hey! If it isn’t Shizuku.

189
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Hello.

190
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
-Has the other new addition arrived yet?
-Dunno.

191
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:00,000
You should ask Machi.

192
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
[Dalzollene] This is for September.

193
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:34,000
What’s this? Seems like there’s a lot.

194
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,000
It is.

195
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Both Mister Trink and Mister Rottfelli
would like their fortunes told.

196
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Aw… That sucks.

197
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
I told you I was gonna quit
if you added any more.

198
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,000
And I do apologize.

199
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Your father counts them both
among his closest associates.

200
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:54,000
Well? Where is Papa, anyway?

201
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
He had a very pressing meeting
to attend to.

202
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,000
He’s probably off hunting or playing golf.

203
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:01,000
[line ringing]

204
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Papa? This is Neon.

205
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,000
What? No way!
You can’t fool me that easily!

206
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:11,000
No. No!

207
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Huh?

208
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
Hmm...

209
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Fine, if you keep your word.

210
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
But break one more promise,
and I’ll quit for real!

211
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Hooray! I’m getting
another piece of treasure!

212
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,000
[chuckles] Sweet deal, huh?

213
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Well, congratulations.

214
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:33,000
‘Kay… now that that’s settled,
I’ll get this over with.

215
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:41,000
LOVELY GHOSTWRITER:
ANGELIC AUTO WRITING

216
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
[Basho] I heard somewhere
that she’s an incredible fortune teller.

217
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Thanks to her father’s connections,

218
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:11,000
she’s got some VIP clients
in the underworld.

219
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,000
You have it backwards.

220
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,000
That so?

221
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:18,000
I’d say that the father has used
his daughter

222
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:21,000
to increase his standing
and move up in the underworld.

223
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
And that’s why the prospect of losing her

224
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
is so frightening to him.

225
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:31,000
He’s afraid his enemies might retaliate
by targeting his daughter.

226
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Okay, all done.

227
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Here.

228
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Excellent work.

229
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:41,000
Tomorrow’s auction starts at night,
doesn’t it?

230
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
I want to go shopping beforehand.

231
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:46,000
If that’s what you want,
I shall accompany you.

232
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:02,000
How many years has it been, I wonder…

233
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
since all 13 of the Troupe members
got together?

234
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Feitan?

235
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Three years, two months.

236
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
But two have changed since then.

237
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:16,000
Numbers four and eight
are different.

238
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Machi. Do you...

239
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,000
think number four, Hisoka,
will actually show up?

240
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:23,000
No idea.

241
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:25,000
Don't ask me.

242
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:27,000
[Franklin] Wasn't he your responsibility?

243
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
I just told him to be here.

244
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:32,000
[Feitan] I don't like Hisoka.

245
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Why does the boss let him do
as he pleases?

246
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:37,000
For his skills, probably.

247
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
[snorts] Skills?

248
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Well, his Bungee Gum
is certainly very impressive.

249
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
It would be difficult
for anyone to counter.

250
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:50,000
[Feitan] Are you saying
that the boss is afraid of Hisoka?

251
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Watch yourself.

252
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
[Nobunaga] That’s not what I meant.

253
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,000
Quit being generous.

254
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
You’re giving the guy way too much credit.

255
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,000
[scoffs]

256
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
Talk is as cheap as it ever was.

257
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Shut up...

258
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
or this is what happens, Nobunaga.

259
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
You were talking just
as much as I was, Franklin.

260
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
-Here we go again.
-[Feitan] Ignore them.

261
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:24,000
They’re just playing around.

262
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
[Machi] So, why is the chief
calling everyone together, anyway?

263
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[Feitan] We’re thieves,

264
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:34,000
I assume he wants us to steal something.

265
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[Machi] Well, that much I know.

266
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
[Dalzollene] Yes.
We’ve arrived safely at the hotel.

267
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:47,000
But one of the young mistress’s fortunes
concerns me…

268
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:53,000
“In the basement where prices rise,
your bed shall be made with your brothers.

269
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Do not descend stairs
you have never climbed.

270
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,000
In numbers, do not compete with others.”

271
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:03,000
And there are three other poems
that begin with the same verse,

272
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:05,000
meaning that all four of the clients

273
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
received fortunes
that are nearly identical.

274
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:11,000
It seems the only thing
that connects them

275
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
is that at this year’s
Underground Auction,

276
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:15,000
each one of them will be attending.

277
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:19,000
[Nostrade] So, the fortune says
their lives are at risk,

278
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,000
should they choose to participate?

279
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:25,000
I think the "sleep" imagery is a metaphor

280
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
for illness or for death.

281
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
[Nostrade] Understood.

282
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
I will pass the fortunes
along to the clients.

283
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:34,000
There’s one more thing, sir…

284
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,000
The young mistress is never able

285
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,000
to remember the fortunes she’s told,

286
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
and she cannot tell her own.

287
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Does it make sense
to let her take part in the auction?

288
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[Nostrade] No! Bring her back immediately!

289
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,000
However, without a proper explanation,
she won’t listen to a word I say.

290
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:57,000
And if she throws a tantrum,
we won’t be able to stop her.

291
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,000
[laughs]

292
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:01,000
In any case,
do not take her to the auction.

293
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Send some bodyguards
to place the bids instead.

294
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
[Dalzollene] Understood.

295
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
[sighs heavily]

296
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[Nostrade] Neon...

297
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
[Phinks clicking tongue]
He isn’t coming.

298
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
[Feitan] The sun is almost up.

299
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,000
[Uvogin] Dammit, Hisoka.

300
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:28,000
Next time I see him,
I’ll tear him apart.

301
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,000
[Hisoka] Oh, dear…

302
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:37,000
That sounds quite gruesome indeed.

303
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
I’m simply terrified.

304
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Hisoka, you bastard!

305
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Guess you’re running a bit late.

306
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:46,000
[Machi]
I was starting to think you wouldn’t show.

307
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Why wouldn’t I?
You asked me to come, didn’t you?

308
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Had I broken my promise,

309
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:57,000
I would never have the pleasure
of seeing your Nen Stitches again.

310
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
-[Machi snorts]
-Okay, boss. Everyone’s here!

311
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
Well, boss?
What are we stealing this time?

312
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
We will take the treasures
of the Underground Auction.

313
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Which treasures do you want?

314
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:20,000
Ancient texts, maybe?

315
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:22,000
The boss does like books.

316
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:25,000
[Feitan] No. But perhaps games.

317
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:30,000
There will be many copies
of the most expensive game ever.

318
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Wouldn’t it be more logical
to take precious metals and gemstones?

319
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,000
[boss] All of it.

320
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:39,000
We'll be taking everything
that's up for auction.

321
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Hold on, boss.
Are you serious?

322
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:49,000
The Underground Auction is operated
by gangs from all over the world!

323
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Just think about it!

324
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:55,000
If we do that, we’re gonna make enemies
out of every last one of ‘em!

325
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:58,000
Are you scared, Uvogin?

326
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
No way! I’m ecstatic!

327
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:04,000
I can’t stop shaking!

328
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Come on! Give us the order, boss!

329
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
I want it now!

330
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,000
I give you permission to kill them all.

331
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
Anyone who dares to get in our way.

332
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
[Uvogin roaring]

333
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
[Dalzollene] Good work.

334
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:32,000
I have your next assignment.

335
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
You must win the three items on this list
at the Underground Auction.

336
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Money is no object.

337
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:45,000
The intact mummy of Princess Corco.

338
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,000
A tissue used by the actor

339
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:51,000
Sonne Limarch,
with a certificate of DNA authenticity.

340
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,000
-[groans]
-[Dalzollene] And...

341
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:58,000
the eyes of a Kurta,
known as the Scarlet Eyes.

342
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,000
[shuddering breath]

343
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
Also, we’ve received information

344
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:07,000
that there might be an attack
on the auction.

345
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,000
So be prepared for any contingency,

346
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
but keep your focus
on the primary objective

347
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
of obtaining these items.

348
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:23,000
They're coming.

349
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
They’re definitely coming!

350
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:32,000
[narrator] Kurapika eagerly awaits
his revenge against the Phantom Troupe,

351
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
a band of murdering thieves.

352
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
The sun has risen
on the first day of the auction,

353
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,000
where all sides will soon collide.

354
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:47,000
[theme song playing]

355
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,000
[Gon] Coming up:

356
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

357
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

358
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

359
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[both] And this is Hunterpedia!

360
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,000
Today, we’re introducing Neon,

361
00:23:01,000 --> 00:23:02,000
the daughter of the head
of the Nostrade family.

362
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
She’s a Flesh Collector!

363
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Her Nen ability’s
the "Lovely Ghostwriter."

364
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,000
I think I’d try to tell my own fortune.

365
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
[Gon] Turns out you can’t do that.

366
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
[Gon] Next time: "Defend x And x Attack"!

367
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Killua! Are you better
at defending or attacking?

368
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
-[Killua] What do you think?
-[Gon] Um... attacking?

369
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
[Killua] Bingo.
